    },
    {
      "content": "Given:\n- Diana gets 30 minutes of video game time for every hour she reads.\n- Her dad decided to raise her reward by 20%.\n- Diana read for 12 hours this week.\n\nUnknown:\n- How many more minutes of video game time will she get as a result of the raise?\n\nFirst, calculate the original reward per hour:\n\\[ \\text{Original reward} = 30 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\]\n\nNext, calculate the increased reward per hour after a 20% raise:\n\\[ \\text{Increase} = 30 \\times 0.20 = 6 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\\[ \\text{New reward} = 30 + 6 = 36 \\text{ minutes/hour} \\]\n\nNow, calculate the total video game time Diana gets for reading 12 hours:\n\\[ \\text{Total time} = 12 \\times 36 = 432 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nCalculate the total time she would have gotten without the raise:\n\\[ \\text{Total time without raise} = 12 \\times 30 = 360 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nFind the difference to determine how many more minutes she gets as a result of the raise:\n\\[ \\text{Difference} = 432 - 360 = 72 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nThus, Diana gets 72 more minutes of video game time as a result of the raise.\n\nFINAL: 72",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
  "student_prefix_sha256": "e1cba70f1aee545718e18c463776f4000d3807520f416f20a7d024b315a7dc8d",
  "target": "Given:\n- Diana gets 30 minutes of video game time for every hour she reads.\n- Her dad decided to raise her reward by 20%.\n- Diana read for 12 hours this week.\n\nUnknown:\n- How many more minutes of video game time will she get as a result of the raise?\n\nOperations:\n1. Calculate the original reward per hour.\n2. Apply the 20% raise to the original reward.\n3. Calculate the total video game time with the new reward.\n4. Calculate the total video game time with the original reward.\n5. Find the difference between the new and original total video game times.\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n1. Original reward per hour: 30 minutes.\n2. New reward per hour after 20% raise: \\(30 \\times 1.20 = 36\\) minutes.\n3. Total video game time with new reward: \\(12 \\times 36 = 432\\) minutes.\n4. Total video game time with original reward: \\(12 \\times 30 = 360\\) minutes.\n5. Difference in video game time: \\(432 - 360 = 72\\) minutes.\n\nCheck:\n- Original reward: 30 minutes/hour.\n- New reward: 36 minutes/hour.\n- Hours read: 12 hours.\n- Total time with new reward: \\(12 \\times 36 = 432\\) minutes.\n- Total time with original reward: \\(12 \\times 30 = 360\\) minutes.\n- Difference: \\(432 - 360 = 72\\) minutes.\n\nThus, Diana gets 72 more minutes of video game time as a result of the raise.\n\nFINAL: 72",
